# colocar som de despertador
# #audio "res://arts/musics/electronic-alarm-clock.mp3" [volume="-5.5"]
[background arg="res://arts/splash art/big text on screen/chapter 1.png" fade="0.0"]
[wait_input]
[background arg="res://arts/splash art/splash arts/place holder 11.png" fade="0.5"]
My mind becomes blank. I wake with a start. The hairs on my skin are all raised. My heart is beating faster. I feel energized after that strange dream.
fade out
fade in
[background arg="res://arts/splash art/splash arts/place holder 12.png" fade="0.5"]
I am back a the medical lab. I am more used to making the rounds, gathering reports from my assistants, and checking up on all the specimens in the inventory.
[background arg="res://arts/splash art/splash arts/place holder 13.png" fade="0.5"]
Once again, I approach L3XA.
It feels different this time. I stare at their serene face, and it somehow looks familiar. being here, right next to it, I feel in the air a familiar sensation that I can’t quite describe.
The specimen also seems to be reacting to my approach. The closer I get, the more I see its facial muscles twitching. It relaxes when I walk away from it.
The computer monitor shows some alteration in the metabolic processes. It’s nothing alarming, but it’s enough to go on my hourly report to the bridge.
I continue my rounds, absent-mindedly, when something else unusual happens.
stranger: “So it’s you then, that I saw the other night.”
This voice. I recognize it.
I look around, trying to find the person who spoke to me. Nobody is paying attention.
stranger: “I didn’t expect we would meet here, of all places.”
My eyes turn in the direction of L3XA’s tank. The creature is still static, its eyes are still closed.
alien: “Yes, that's me. Ironic that I can’t see you now, and you couldn’t see me before.”
- Pretend to ignore
	jump chapter 1/PRETEND NOT TO LISTEN
- Respond
	jump chapter 1/LISTEN
label PRETEND NOT TO LISTEN
[background fade="0.5"]
join alien (neutra no tubo) left [mirrored="true"]
join doctor right
After a confused pause, I decide to continue walking as if nothing changed. I don’t know what’s happening right now, and I want to know more before I commit to a reaction.
alien: “Are you listening to me right now? I know you are, you are the only person that can hear me.”
I continue silent, trying not to show any disturbance on my face to any onlookers.
alien: “You were more open to conversation when we first met. But I guess I spooked you. Take you time, and we can talk.”
Is L3XA really referring to last night’s… dream? What was that all about?
alien: “...I guess that you don’t know that you can talk to me like I do. If you form your thoughts in the shape of words and send them to me, I will pick up on them.”
I decide to venture a response.
update doctor [mirrored="true"]
jump chapter 1/main
label LISTEN
[background fade="0.5"]
join alien (neutra no tubo) left [mirrored="true"]
join doctor right [mirrored="true"]
\doctor: “Hey, excuse me?”
Everyone at the lab stares at me. They look confused.
alien: “They can’t hear me, silly. I think it will be best if you keep your cool.”
I guess I should say something so no one thinks I'm crazy.
\doctor: “Uhmmm, I… can somebody get me the results of the last blood test on specimen 000-96?”
# fazer um personagem cientista
scientist: “Yes, Ma’am, right away.”
alien: “That was clever. It should do for now. I have a feeling we would not be able to talk for too long if they knew that I am awake.”
\doctor: “...”
alien: “ There is a way you can talk to me as I’m talking to you now. Listen\: try to form the words that you want to say in your mind and send them to me. Can you do that?”
So I can just communicate with L3XA via telepathy? I should try it. There’s so much going through my head right now.
label main
\doctor: “...can you hear me…?”
alien: “Yes, I can hear you. It’s been so long since I heard someone talking to me like this.”
\doctor: “This is very new to me… can we talk? I have some questions.”
alien: “Go ahead. Ask me anything.”
\doctor: “Okay so… how do you do this? The telepathy, I mean.”
alien: “It’s how my species communicates. However, in this state, I can’t hold our connection for very long.
alien: I would like to talk to you all day, but for now we only have some time before I slip into unconsciousness again.”
